From af4af60f56910fc655b12757408fbf428400b2bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:49:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Apply the atmospheric pressure to the nested ocean
 (workaround for #676)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The coupled model sets the ocean's barotropic potential (atmospheric pressure / ρ₀) through
forcing_barotropic_potential(coupled_model.ocean), which has no method for a NestedModel and falls
back to nothing: since #43 no nested run has had the atmospheric pressure, and #676's inverse-
barometer sea level, read from the same field, stayed zero (the smoke test with inverse_barometer
= true was bit-for-bit identical to the one without). nested_pressure_fix.jl forwards the call to
the child, which holds the pressure forcing. This changes results: the JRA55 pressure now acts on
the ocean, with the inverse barometer on GLORYS's η at the open sides and in the initial state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Abhhvkp8Pai9cvvctGUDX5
---
 nested_pressure_fix.jl | 8 ++++++++
 panarctic.jl           | 1 +
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 nested_pressure_fix.jl

diff --git a/nested_pressure_fix.jl b/nested_pressure_fix.jl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..879baf3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/nested_pressure_fix.jl
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+# Workaround for NumericalEarth #676 (nested_ocean_model): the coupled model applies the atmosphere's pressure to the
+# ocean through `forcing_barotropic_potential(coupled_model.ocean)`, which has no method for a NestedModel, so it falls
+# back to `nothing` and the pressure is never applied to a nested ocean. The child's barotropic potential then stays
+# zero, and so does #676's inverse-barometer sea level (`inverse_barometer = true` changes nothing). Forward the call
+# to the child, which holds the pressure forcing. To be fixed in #676; remove this file then.
+
+NumericalEarth.Oceans.forcing_barotropic_potential(model::NumericalEarth.NestedModels.NestedModel) =
+    NumericalEarth.Oceans.forcing_barotropic_potential(model.child)
diff --git a/panarctic.jl b/panarctic.jl
index fa2054b..cd72d01 100644
--- a/panarctic.jl
+++ b/panarctic.jl
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 
 include("setup.jl")
 include("jra55_read_fix.jl")
+include("nested_pressure_fix.jl")
 
 # Mass-consistent momentum advection at partial bottom cells (Oceananigans.jl#6533), before the model is built
 get(config["grid"], "partial_cell_fix", false) && grid.immersed_boundary isa PartialCellBottom && include("partial_cell_fix.jl")
